  "comparison": "exact",
  "note": "The first family of operations: create, set, clear and the two renames. A refused batch answers with the objects it was given rather than with what it had reached, so a case that refuses reads as the proof that nothing was written. A rename of a variable is the one that reaches furthest: the slot moves, and so do the trees of every formula that read it, the markers inside a text object, the address macros of a math source, and the target a copy carries outside the slot set.",
